| actual edge | next vertex | cross x | cross y | cross z |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| 1 | 2 | -1 | -1 | 1 |
| 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
\image(figures/newell_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual translated edge contributions for the original tilted triangle.)
\alttext(The nonzero cross product is(−1,−1,1); the normalized vector comes from the same producer.)

> Retain all three original polygons

The original square in z=0 has unit normal(0,0,1) and area4. The figure
explicitly shows its xy projection: the normal points out of the page, so its xy
components cannot form a visible in-plane arrow. The printed values are actual
native results for the square, triangle and original tilted quad. The native
fixture preserves all their original coordinates.

The original quad is(0,0,0),(2,0,.1),(2,2,0),(0,2,−.1). These vertices share the
plane z=.05x−.05y; calling it “slightly non-planar” was incorrect. Its native
signed distances to the centroid plane are near rounding zero. This is a useful
tilted planar control rather than evidence of behavior on warped input.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/newell_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/newell_normal.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto fixtures = dm::algorithms::newell_demo_polygons();
    std::print("| original case | actual unit x | actual unit y | actual unit z | vector-area magnitude | " "maximum centroid-plane distance |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
        auto a = dm::algorithms::newell_analyze(fixtures[i].polygon);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", fixtures[i].name,
                   a.unit[0], a.unit[1], a.unit[2], a.vector_area,
                   a.max_plane_distance);
    }
    auto a = dm::algorithms::newell_analyze(fixtures[0].polygon);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (auto &v : fixtures[0].polygon) {
        x.push_back(v[0]);
        y.push_back(v[1]);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.polygon(x, y, {213, 226, 249}).points(x, y, "square vertices",
                                            {36, 105, 172}, 5).text(
        1, 1,
        std::format("Actual n=({:.0f},{:.0f},{:.0f})\nout of xy page",
                    a.unit[0], a.unit[1], a.unit[2]), {17, 24, 39}, 14).size(
        850, 850).margins(95, 35, 60, 70).x_limits(-.5, 2.5).y_limits(-.5, 2.5).title("Original planar square: explicit xy projection").x_label("x").y_label("y").save_svg("build/newell_original.svg");
}
