> A genuinely warped quad and an honest plane diagnostic

Changing only the fourth vertex’s z coordinate from−.1 to.3 makes the quad
nonplanar. The native diagnostic plane passes through the arithmetic centroid
and uses the returned Newell unit direction. Signed distances quantify how this
specific plane represents the supplied vertices; it is not asserted to minimize
squared distances or furnish a supporting plane. The two panels use identical
signed-distance limits. Near-zero values for the original quad and nonzero
values for the corrected control separate the experiments directly.

No unique scalar surface area follows from a nonplanar boundary alone. Choosing
a diagonal, triangulated mesh or spanning surface adds information that this API
does not receive. Consequently the reported scalar keeps the name vector-area
magnitude throughout the warped experiment.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/newell_warped.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/newell_normal.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto fixtures = dm::algorithms::newell_demo_polygons();
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
    std::print("| case | actual maximum absolute plane distance | actual vector-area magnitude |\n| --- | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int index : {2, 3}) {
        auto a = dm::algorithms::newell_analyze(fixtures[index].polygon);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", fixtures[index].name,
                   a.max_plane_distance, a.vector_area);
        auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
        p.points({0, 1, 2, 3}, a.signed_plane_distances, "signed distance",
                 {36, 105, 172}, 5).abline_h(0, {192, 59, 50}, 1).title(
            fixtures[index].name).x_label("original vertex index").y_label(
            "centroid-plane signed distance").y_limits(-.15, .15);
        layout.add(p);
    }
    layout.size(1200, 600).fit_panels().save_svg("build/newell_warped.svg");
}
